WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:02.330
(upbeat music)

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:06.056
- [Narrator] Inside this 250
ton three headed elephant

00:00:06.056 --> 00:00:09.520
is a museum commissioned
as a place to preserve

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.940
Thai heritage.
(upbeat music)

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:20.860
The Erawan Museum is located
just outside of Bangkok.

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:23.600
It is named and inspired
by the mythological king

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:25.650
of elephants in Hindu mythology.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:30.470
Inside there is a large temple
in the belly of the elephant.

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:34.260
And downstairs is a museum
which features carvings inspired

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:37.633
by Buddhism, Christianity, and Hinduism.

00:00:37.633 --> 00:00:40.252
(upbeat music)

00:00:40.252 --> 00:00:43.450
Outside a walk around the
landscaped paths feature model

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:46.332
elephants that trumpet as
guests walk under them.

00:00:46.332 --> 00:00:47.720
(elephant trumpet)

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:50.940
With thousands of visitors
every year, the museum serves

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:52.860
as a tribute to Thailand's past.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:57.213
(gentle music)

